  The reel_script and slides say the 17th and 24th meetings will not be held, but the article only says the 17th was cancelled last week and the 24th is 'today' (the article's own date context); the reel_script's 'இன்று 24ஆம் தேதி' wording is a stretch but mostly consistent.
  Slide 'ஏன் ரத்து?' states the meeting is cancelled this week because the commissioner is going for training; the article gives this reason, but the slide and reel_script merge it with the 17th/24th cancellation without clarifying which reason applies to which date (mixing facts).
  The reel_script says 'மேயர் ... கடந்த வாரம் ஏன் ரத்தானது என்று நினைவில் இல்லை' (mayor does not remember why last week was cancelled) and the slide 'மேயர் விளக்கம்' lists only the local-presence point; the claim that the mayor is 'the only' spokesperson is not an error, but the slide omits her Diwali explanation for the 10th, which is an important cause fact.
  The slide 'மக்கள் புகார்' says people 'ஏமாந்து திரும்புவதாகக் கேள்வி' – the article says people ask questions and return disappointed, which is roughly consistent, but the slide's 'வாரத்துக்கு 50 முதல் 100 மனுக்கள்' is presented as a current fact rather than the average when meetings do happen, which is acceptable.
